{# ===========================================================================
   Component: the Hours row of the NAP plate.

   One implementation for all three location templates. The row used to be
   written out separately in each, which is how Convoy ended up with no Hours
   row at all while the other two carried "Being confirmed. Call the room."

   Expects `loc` in scope. Takes one optional variable, `hoursLabel`, which
   defaults to "Hours".

   WHY THE LABEL IS A VARIABLE. /happy-hour/ renders this component beside a
   happy hour window, and on that page "Hours" alone is dangerous: two sets of
   times on one card, one of which is a discount window and one of which is
   when the door is open, and a reader who conflates them leaves thinking the
   discount runs until close. That page passes "The room is open". The location
   pages pass nothing and read "Hours" as before.

   Hours confirmed 2026-09-09 by Connor for six of seven. Maui was not
   supplied, so it keeps the honest fallback rather than borrowing a sibling's
   pattern: CLIENT_FACTS.md's rule is do not publish hours the door does not
   honor, and that has not changed for Maui.

   Days come from the `dayRange` filter, times straight from locations.json.
   The same array feeds openingHoursSpecification in _data/schema.js, so the
   visible row and the graph cannot drift.
   =========================================================================== #}
<span class="plate__item">
  <span class="plate__label">{{ hoursLabel | default("Hours") }}</span>
  {%- if loc.hours and loc.hours.length %}
  <span class="plate__value plate__value--hours">
    {%- for rule in loc.hours %}
    <span class="plate__hours-row">
      <span class="plate__hours-days">{{ rule.days | dayRange }}</span>
      <span class="plate__hours-time">{{ rule.opens | clockTime }} to {{ rule.closes | clockTime }}</span>
    </span>
    {%- endfor %}
  </span>
  {#
    THE LIVE STATUS. Ships hidden and empty, and /src/js/hours.js fills it
    from the same `hours` array rendered above, computed in
    America/Los_Angeles because whether a room is open is a fact about San
    Diego rather than about the reader.

    An ENHANCEMENT: with JavaScript off this renders nothing at all and the
    published hours above it are untouched. It is never a replacement for
    them, and it is deliberately absent from schema.
    openingHoursSpecification is server-rendered from this same array in
    _data/schema.js and stays the canonical answer.

    Times match the rows directly above. Both are 12-hour, via the clockTime
    filter here and the matching formatter in hours.js: "Open until 10pm"
    beside "11:30am to 10pm" reads as one fact. The raw 24-hour values stay in
    locations.json and stay in openingHoursSpecification, which is where ISO
    time belongs.

    Maui has no `hours`, so it renders no status element at all rather than a
    fallback string, which is the same rule its "Call the room" row follows.
  #}
  <span class="plate__status" data-hours-status data-hours='{{ loc.hours | dump }}' hidden></span>
  {%- else %}
  <span class="plate__value">Call the room</span>
  {%- endif %}
</span>
